    "text": "<p>A black coloured solid sphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;is inside a cavity with a vacuum inside. The walls of the cavity are maintained at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. The initial temperature of the sphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. If the specific heat of the material of the sphere varies as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;per unit mass with the temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> of the sphere, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is a constant, then the time taken for the sphere to cool down to temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> will be<br /><br />(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#963;</mi></math>&nbsp;is Stefan Boltzmann constant)</p>"
